      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(canvas): surface eval errors instead of silently swallowing them",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen `canvas.eval` returns a non-string result or error from the node (e.g. `{ payload: { error: \"SyntaxError: Unexpected token\" } }`), the old code returned `jsonResult({ ok: true })` — a generic success signal. The agent sees success even when the JavaScript evaluation failed.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe `raw` cast at `tool.ts:160-162` only recognized `{ payload?: { result?: string } }`. When `result` was absent or non-string (number, null, undefined), control fell through to `return jsonResult({ ok: true })`. Gateway errors in other payload shapes were silently discarded.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Type cast widened to `{ payload?: { result?: unknown; error?: string } }`\n- Non-string results return `{ ok: false, error, result }` so error context is visible to the agent\n- String results are unchanged (existing behavior preserved)\n\nFiles changed:\n- `extensions/canvas/src/tool.ts`: Refactored `case \"eval\"` handler\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: Non-string eval results and errors are now surfaced instead of silently swallowed\n- Commands / artifacts:\n  - `git diff main --check -- extensions/canvas/` — clean\n  - `npx vitest run extensions/canvas/src/tool.test.ts` — 12 passed, 1 skipped (symlink on Windows)\n- Observed result: All existing tests pass. Non-string results correctly return `{ ok: false, error, result }`.",
        "branch": "fix/canvas-eval-silent-failure",
